From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 04:43:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] package the vendored ruamel.yaml licence with the wheels

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap is in every srsly 2.x wheel on PyPI and srsly 3.0.0 unvendors the library altogether, so this needs a maintainer decision on the 2.x line rather than a drive-by PR]

srsly vendors ruamel.yaml under srsly/ruamel_yaml and ships it in every
wheel, but srsly/ruamel_yaml/LICENSE is not packaged: MANIFEST.in only
recurses over source files and PACKAGE_DATA only globs *.pyx/*.pxd/*.c/
*.h/*.cpp, so the wheel carries srsly's own MIT LICENSE alone. None of
the vendored ruamel.yaml modules carries a copyright header either, so
nothing in the wheel reproduces the notice its MIT licence requires to
travel with copies.

The other vendored trees do not have this problem -- ujson, msgpack and
cloudpickle each keep their full licence text in the sources that ship in
the wheel (srsly/ujson/lib/ultrajson.h, srsly/msgpack/pack.h,
srsly/cloudpickle/cloudpickle.py).

Copying the file to the project root as LICENSE.ruamel_yaml needs no
packaging change: setuptools' default license_files glob is LICEN[CS]E*
at the root, so it lands in the wheel's dist-info/licenses/ beside
srsly's own.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.ruamel_yaml | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.ruamel_yaml

diff --git a/LICENSE.ruamel_yaml b/LICENSE.ruamel_yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5b863d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.ruamel_yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
